Subject: [PATCH] apk: journal transactions and resume interrupted commits

Before the first package write on a live root, keep a durable journal under
lib/apk/db/transaction: the target world, exact package identities, the
signed indexes and copies of the verified payloads. The journal is removed
once the database, post-commit hooks and kernel policy have completed.

While a journal is pending other commits are refused. "apk fix
--openwrt-resume" solves the journaled transaction again with solver-local
identity constraints, requires the same changes and commits them; when the
database was already written it reruns only the post-commit hooks and
kernel policy. APK_OPENWRT_JOURNAL enables the journal for --root tests.

---
--- a/doc/apk-fix.8.scd
+++ b/doc/apk-fix.8.scd
@@ -24,6 +24,14 @@
 *--directory-permissions*
 	Reset all directory permissions.
 
+*--openwrt-resume*
+	Finish a package transaction that was interrupted after it started
+	writing (power loss, crash or SIGKILL). The transaction journal in
+	_/lib/apk/db/transaction_ records the target world, the exact package
+	identities and the indexes used; the same changes are solved again and
+	committed. When only the post-commit actions were cut off, they run
+	again. Other APK commits are refused while a journal is pending.
+
 *--reinstall*, *-r*
 	Reinstall packages (default).
 
